\description{
Turns each recording into one row, with frames in a list column and a
transcript beside them. \code{measure(text = , image = )} then reads both on the
same call, since they are two columns of one row rather than two objects to
align.

The audio half is \code{\link[=prepare_audio]{prepare_audio()}} unchanged, running on a wav \code{ffmpeg}
extracts.
}
\section{Choosing frames}{

\code{select = "uniform"} divides the recording into \code{frames} equal segments and
takes the middle of each. Midpoints rather than endpoints, since a frame at
exactly zero is often a title card and one at exactly the end is often black.

\code{select = "change"} takes the \code{frames} highest scene scores instead, which
\code{ffmpeg} computes for every frame as how much this picture differs from the
one before it. It finds cuts that even spacing misses, and it concentrates.
\code{min_gap} is what stops that, and it exists only for this mode.
}

\section{Recordings without audio}{

\code{ffprobe} is asked whether an audio stream exists before anything is
extracted. Where there is none, the row comes back with its frames and with
\code{has_audio = FALSE}, \code{text} and every audio count \code{NA}, and the count is
reported. A batch of campaign advertisements does not stop because three of
them are silent.

\code{exists} and \code{has_audio} answer different questions and both are needed.\tabular{llll}{
   case \tab \code{exists} \tab \code{has_audio} \tab \code{text} \cr
   file not found \tab \code{FALSE} \tab \code{NA} \tab \code{NA} \cr
   present, silent \tab \code{TRUE} \tab \code{FALSE} \tab \code{NA} \cr
   present, with audio \tab \code{TRUE} \tab \code{TRUE} \tab the transcript \cr
}


\code{NA} on \code{has_audio} is doing work. The file was never opened, so \code{FALSE}
would assert something that was not checked.

\code{n_words} is \code{NA} for a silent recording rather than \code{0}, because nothing
was transcribed. A recording whose audio track is silence is a different
thing, gets transcribed, and comes back with \code{n_words = 0}.

Every other audio column is \code{NA} there too, \code{diarized} and \code{tool} and
\code{asr_model} included. Nothing ran, so there is nothing to report and naming
a model would assert settings that produced no words.
}

\section{Frame storage}{

On disk in \verb{<stem>_frames/} inside \code{cache_dir}, because \code{measure(image = )}
reads paths.

The wav lands beside it, which is what lets \code{\link[=prepare_audio]{prepare_audio()}}'s cache work
unchanged. The frames keep a record of their own, \verb{<stem>_frames.fathom.json}
in the frames directory, holding the times they were cut at and the JPEG
quality. Changing \code{frames}, \code{select}, \code{include_first}, \code{min_gap} or \code{quality}
changes that record, so every frame is cut again and the old pictures are
removed, while the transcript is read back from its own cache.
}

